# symoneural-discovery credentials — the TEMPLATE. Every value here is empty and must stay
# empty: this file is tracked, so a real key pasted below is a key in the git history,
# and
# backend/apps/test_credential_header.py asserts that every credential-shaped name in a
# tracked *.example file has no value.
#
# cp symoneural-discovery.env.example symoneural-discovery.env     # then edit
# symoneural-discovery.env
#
# symoneural-discovery.env is excluded by .gitignore:135. The loader reads it automatically
# (envfile.py), so this is a one-time edit rather than an export every session. Anything
# already set in the shell wins over this file — see envfile.load().
#
# Nothing below is required to run `stats`, `export`, `search --backends duckduckgo`, or
# `crawl`. Fill in a key when you want the backend it unlocks.

# --- Search backend: pick ONE for --backends -----------------------------

# Google Programmable Search Engine (Custom Search JSON API). Two values, from two different
# consoles, and the pairing is the part that catches people out:
#   console.cloud.google.com          -> enable "Custom Search API" -> Credentials -> API key
#   programmablesearchengine.google.com -> create engine, toggle "Search the entire web" -> ID
# Free tier is 100 queries/day; past that the Cloud project needs billing enabled.
GOOGLE_CSE_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_CSE_CX=

# Bing Web Search API. UNVERIFIED ON THIS BOX and possibly unobtainable: Microsoft retired
# the standalone Bing Search APIs in mid-2025 in favour of "Grounding with Bing Search",
# which is scoped to Azure AI Agent Service rather than a key you drop into a script. The
# `bing` backend in discovery.py still speaks the classic api.bing.microsoft.com shape, so if
# a new sign-up cannot produce a key for that endpoint the backend is dead code and should be
# deleted rather than left looking available. Nobody has tested it here.
BING_SEARCH_API_KEY=

# SerpApi (serpapi.com) — third-party aggregator, key shown on the dashboard.
SERPAPI_API_KEY=

# The duckduckgo backend needs no key and is the default. See its docstring for the caveats:
# no SLA, undocumented rate limits, markup that can change without notice.

# --- Answer synthesis (only the `answer` subcommand and --expand > 1) ----

# console.anthropic.com -> Settings -> API Keys. Billed pay-as-you-go and separate from a
# claude.ai subscription; a payment method must be on file before the key does real work.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Not read by discovery.py — carried here for other tooling ----------
# These two are in the file because Garrett asked for them, not because anything in this
# package looks them up. `grep -rn HF_TOKEN backend/` returns nothing but this template and
# its test. If a later tool starts reading them, say so here.

HF_TOKEN=
GITHUB_TOKEN=
